Source: homelab-dns
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Jeff Gardner <mailmasker-api01@forge.name>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/permittivity2/homelab

Package: homelab-dns
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, pdns-server, pdns-backend-pgsql, postgresql-client, adduser
Description: PowerDNS authoritative DNS provisioning for the homelab-* ecosystem
 Wires PowerDNS's PostgreSQL (gpgsql) backend via the native pdns.d
 drop-in directory -- never edits pdns.conf directly. Supports a real
 primary/secondary (master/slave) topology. Applies the official
 upstream schema (referenced from the installed pdns-backend-pgsql
 package, not vendored/duplicated) only if it isn't already present,
 and never touches any other tenant of the same database. PowerDNS
 keeps its own dedicated `powerdns` database with its own conventional
 role -- unlike the Perl homelab-* features, it is not part of the
 shared `homelab` database / split-role bootstrap design (see
 CLAUDE.md) since its schema/migration lifecycle is owned upstream by
 the PowerDNS project itself, not by this ecosystem.
